/target
**/target
/web/node_modules
/web/.svelte-kit
/web/build
.env
.env.local
*.log
.DS_Store
/data
/docker/garage-*
# Local agent/editor state. `scheduled_tasks.lock` was committed by accident and is
# runtime bookkeeping, not configuration anybody else can use.
/.claude

# Local credential scratch files. `.sec` was sitting untracked and un-ignored in a repository
# about to go public — one `git add -A` from being committed. Ignoring the pattern rather than
# the one filename, because the next one will be called something else.
.sec
*.sec
secrets.env

# Terraform. `.terraform/` is downloaded providers — the AWS one alone is 780MB, which GitHub rejects
# outright, and it took a rejected push to find out that the ignore rule was sitting on an unmerged
# branch while `git add -A` ran on this one. State is worse than the providers: it holds whatever the
# resources contain, which is why `terraform/nightly-ci` deliberately creates no access key.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
crash.log
